     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, <div><br></div><div>I am designing a shiny app with multiple interactive inputs including a textArea. I want to make this textArea respond only after a user finished typing multiple keywords (in multiple lines). I do not want to use submit button, so am thinking of making the textArea&#39;s response time delayed by 1-2 seconds.  </div><div><br></div><div>Simply I want to make my textArea act like this:</div><div><br></div><div>abc (enter)<br></div><div>cbd (enter)</div><div>dsd (enter)</div><div>[if there is no input for 2 seconds after the 3rd word, textArea finally sends these three words as a single string vector to the server] </div><div><br></div><div>It is possible?  Could you share your idea with me? You may edit the following backbone code.</div><div><br></div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(76,136,107);font-style:italic;font-family:&quot;Source Code Pro&quot;,monospace;font-weight:bold;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">## Only run examples in interactive R sessions</span></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&quot;Source Code Pro&quot;,monospace;font-weight:bold;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(230,230,230)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,255);font-family:&quot;Source Code Pro&quot;,monospace;font-weight:bold;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">if</span></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&quot;Source Code Pro&quot;,monospace;font-weight:bold;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(230,230,230)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,255);font-family:&quot;Source Code Pro&quot;,monospace;font-weight:bold;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">(</span></span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;colo